# std/deep-deps (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): part of the SEEDED core.
# deep-deps rejoins the seeded set because the std-root whole-tree transform
# can't deepen a tree that CONTAINS deep-deps without already having it (cycle-2)
# — so it must resolve without the transform, which a seed does. Like rustc it
# names a distinct sentinel (`docker://seeded-deep-deps`); bootstrap hand-builds
# the result — curry(runner, worker1=<worker-deep-deps binary>) — and seeds it
# under this expression's key. No binary is staged into the checked-in entry.
run --base:docker=seeded-deep-deps --in:@=.
